<!--Post: 714--><!--Time: 1092062775-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST714"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 09, 2004 - 7:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I could have sworn there was a murder victim of this name, in or near Wichita, and the circumstances of her death sounded a bit familiar. <BR>Anyone from the area remember the name Marine Hedge? I may have misspelled the first name but I know &#34;Hedge&#34; is accurate.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 714-->
<!--Post: 716--><!--Time: 1092069788-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST716"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 09, 2004 - 9:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, Marine Hedge is one of the cold cases. Apr, 27, 1985, Park City, no address. Park City is a suburb of Wichita. <BR>-Deb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 716-->
<!--Post: 725--><!--Time: 1092116869-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST725"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, August 09, 2004 - 10:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Flytodeb!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 725-->
<!--Post: 1152--><!--Time: 1097455771-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST1152"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Quell<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Quell<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, October 10, 2004 - 5:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Marine Hedge was a 54 year-old restaurant worker.  This lady would have been carrying money and wearing a food service uniform.  Robbery once again?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 1152-->
<!--Post: 2294--><!--Time: 1103501589-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2294"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 19, 2004 - 4:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/wicoca.html" target=_top>http://members.fortunecity.com/ghostiesannex/wicoc a.html</a> <BR> <BR>&#34;6200 block of Independance, Park City, age 53. Abducted from her home between 1:00 am &amp; 7:00 am after dinner at a restaurant and bingo with her boyfriend. She was found 8 days later along a dirt road, and the autopsy showed she was strangled by hand. She was not bound when found, but a pair of knotted pantyhose was found nearby.  Her phone line was cut, her front door was left open, and her Monte Carlo was found the following Thursday in Wichita in a shopping center near 1st &amp; Woodlawn, with a blanket &amp; bedspread in the trunk. It had apparently been wiped down for fingerprints. It was determined that nothing was stolen from the home itself. Ms. Hedge was not sexually assaulted, but small blood spots were found in the home. She was nude when found, covered with tall grass and an evergreen tree in a ditch on 53rd North, about 3/4 of a mile west of Greenwich Rd. Her purse was found the next day in a ditch near 143rd St. East &amp;  37th St. North by a woman who did not turn it in to police until the following Friday.  Ms.Hedge&#39;s ID was gone, police identified the purse by papers found inside it. Police found evergreen needles in the car, and noted that there were no evergreens near the body other than the one covering her, indicating that it may have been transported to the site.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2294-->
<!--Post: 4620--><!--Time: 1106595022-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4620"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Verm_inve<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Verm_inve<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 11:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/cold_cases/hedge.html" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/c old_cases/hedge.html</a> <BR> <BR>Image of Hedge:  <a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/cold_cases/hedge_lrg.jpg" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/sheriff/operations/c old_cases/hedge_lrg.jpg</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
